{# MODULES ACROSS THE ORGANISATION — what each one puts on THIS page.

   A NAME AND A COUNT, NOT A CATALOGUE. The register of what is installed
   lives in Settings; this card answers the question a reader of the dashboard
   actually has, which is whose figures they are looking at and how much of
   the page each module is responsible for.

   THE ORGANISATION'S OWN CELLS ARE NOT A CONTRIBUTION TO ANYBODY, so they are
   not counted here: the question is what installing a module ADDS. #}
<div class="c" data-w="modules">
    <span class="tab">Modules across the organisation<span class="src">&middot; {{ moduleTable|length }} answering at organisation level</span></span>
    {% if modulesUrl %}<a class="more" href="{{ modulesUrl }}">Settings &middot; Modules &rarr;</a>{% endif %}
    <span class="ao-by next"><i></i>the registry</span>

    {% if moduleTable is empty %}
        <p class="zeb">No module answers at organisation level yet. A module that has an org-wide reading contributes its cells here the day it is installed.</p>
    {% else %}
        <table class="tbl">
            <tr><th>module</th><th>cells on this page</th></tr>
            {% for slug, cells in moduleTable %}
                <tr>
                    <td><b>{{ slug }}</b></td>
                    <td class="g">{{ cells }}</td>
                </tr>
            {% endfor %}
        </table>
    {% endif %}
</div>
